	<item>
		<title>By: Randy Sarafan</title>
		<link>http://fffff.at/gml-recording-machine/comment-page-1/#comment-30319</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Randy Sarafan]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 16 Jun 2011 15:58:33 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://fffff.at/?p=7179#comment-30319</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Oh man. I wish I thought of that.

They should use a Gametrak:
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gametrak

And wear it at the waist. This only uses one string, will give them 3-dimensions, and it is a tank-tough commercial product. The only real challenge would be getting it to talk via USB to the Arduino, but even this could be simply bypassed by taking readings straight off the pots.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Oh man. I wish I thought of that.</p>
<p>They should use a Gametrak:<br />
<a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gametrak" rel="nofollow">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gametrak</a></p>
<p>And wear it at the waist. This only uses one string, will give them 3-dimensions, and it is a tank-tough commercial product. The only real challenge would be getting it to talk via USB to the Arduino, but even this could be simply bypassed by taking readings straight off the pots.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
